evidence.en:
function CouponField() {
  const coupon = useSelector((s) => s.checkout.coupon); // always ""
  return <input value={coupon} />;
}

Console: "You provided a `value` prop to a form field without an `onChange` handler..."
The input is now controlled by a value that never changes: after every keystroke React resets the DOM back to the ___b1___ value. The field is not broken HTML — it is missing the ___b2___ handler that would route keystrokes into the store, or it should use ___b3___ if the intent was only to seed the initial text.

